    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_792943b8dedf0b674758e7b29446573ae0c2ce48d0ef565b6c861d9d98d50797",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The boundary-sign proof for ζ′/ζ turns functional-equation pairing into agreement between ζ and ζ′ zero counts in the left half of the critical strip, while the separate negative-half-plane argument classifies the unavoidable ζ′ zeros there as real zeros interlacing the trivial ζ zeros. Together these results upgrade the strip criterion to the source's strengthened formulation: RH is equivalent to ζ′ having no nonreal zeros with real part below one-half.",
