    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ab415870f1068d9540da5d6434ac1341e850e049dbd549bea300e24d959d84f6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The functional equation introduces an auxiliary J whose reflected zeros represent large-height ζ′ zeros, and the quotient J/ζ makes left-derivative and right-ζ zero displacement comparable by Littlewood's lemma. Boxes around right-side ζ zeros then localize the only possible failures of the favorable real-part sign; joining overlapping boxes into bounded chains permits local rectangle counts, and replacing the chain boundary estimate by a second-moment bound sharpens the comparison enough to obtain the moving-boundary density corollary.",
